[Metro Board file 2026-0759, Motion / Motion Response]
APPROVE Motion by Richardson, Hahn, and Bass that the Board direct the Chief Executive Officer to:

A.	Establish the Southeast Gateway Line Streamlined Approval and Permitting Process Pilot Program to reduce permitting and duplicative review requirements, expedite required approvals, and reduce permitting-related cost and schedule risks. Metro shall continue to coordinate collaboratively with affected jurisdictions and to provide plans and specifications for review and comment, while maintaining responsibility for the final project design and delivery. Metro and the corridor cities should work collaboratively to develop a pilot program;

B.	For local jurisdiction permits and approvals, work with corridor jurisdictions to establish a centralized and expedited process with clear responsibilities, predictable review timelines, concurrent reviews where feasible, and a process to quickly resolve issues that threaten project cost or schedule;

C.	Establish clear accountability and performance measures for the pilot program, including tracking required permits and reviews, processing times, schedule impacts, permitting-related project costs, with the goal of demonstrating measurable improvements in project delivery; and

D.	Report back to the Board within 120 days on implementation of the pilot program, the status of the final agreement with corridor cities, participation by corridor jurisdictions, including the Ports, feedback from corridor cities on the collaborative process, identified barriers, initial results, and recommendations for applying successful elements of the model to other Metro capital projects.
